# Markdown: product vs workspace vs binder

Workspaces are **always private**. That is where the extra Markdown lives.

| Remote | Commit these Markdown files |
| --- | --- |
| **Product** (public or private) | `README.md`, `LICENSE` (or `LICENSE.md`), `CHANGELOG.md`, optional short `AGENTS.md` pointer |
| **Workspace** | the full tree below |
| **Binder** | `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/` (cross-company only). No drafts. No `vendor/`. |

A product may ship a short `AGENTS.md` agent-contract pointer (to
`CONSTRAINTS.md` and the parent workspace's `drafts/` and `docs/`). Do not
put `backlog.md`, `drafts/`, or `docs/` in a product git — `gitignore`
those paths. A leftover file is scratch — move it up in the same turn.

## Workspace tree (same names everywhere)

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `README.md` | workspace face |
| `LICENSE` | licence; omit if none |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | hook owns it |
| `AGENTS.md` | agent contract |
| `backlog.md` | queue |
| `readme.start.md` | install notes |
| `drafts/00.DRAFT.INDEX.md` | index |
| `drafts/NN.DRAFT.*.md` | one topic |
| `drafts/99.NEEDS-ATTENTION.md` | status index |
| `docs/*.md` | settled; `SCREAMING-KEBAB.md` |

Product contracts live in the company workspace (`docs/STOREFRONT-PLAN.md`,
…). Do not invent `README.*.md` or `plan.md` at any root. Brand mark
filenames are fixed and documented in the owning `docs/BRAND-MARKS.md`; do
not put `masstrade_` or `pleware_` in a filename.
